{"availability":"available","full":"Erfan-XRay/Kariz","name":"Kariz","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":33,"forks":13,"created":"2026-09-27T20:28:13Z","updated":"2026-10-11T04:08:09Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://erfan-xray.github.io/Kariz/try/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.125Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.125Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.125Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.125Z","stars":33,"forks":13}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["English · فارسی · Website · Documentation · Live demo · Changelog","Kariz (کاریز) takes its name from the qanats of Iran: channels dug under the desert that carry water from the mountains to the villages, through a line of wells, without ever coming to the surface. The software does the same for traffic. It joins two servers with a fast, encrypted tunnel; your users connect to the entry, and Kariz carries their TCP and UDP traffic to the exit, which reaches the real destinations.","It is one small Rust program (about 8 MiB of memory per side, no garbage collector), and a web panel to run it: servers, tunnels, charts and logs in a browser."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Erfan-XRay/Kariz/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9319c2d4a37364c5e07ae8c7e87c7723bdb3738664e430df9680d4095701689e","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.210Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:28.210Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"English · فارسی · Website · Documentation · Live demo · Changelog","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Erfan-XRay/Kariz/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Choose Install the web panel here: it prints the panel's address and a one-time login link.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Erfan-XRay/Kariz/blob/main/README.md"}]